Label
The label for a bar is the direction of future price movement. If the price is higher after InpMlpHorizon bars, the label is class 1 (up); if it is lower, the label is class 0 (down). With series indexing, the future bar is at shift − Horizon (a more recent bar), and when shift > Horizon, it has already closed, so there is no look-ahead bias: at training time, the outcome is known from historical data. The InpLabelMinPts parameter filters out bars with movement below a specified threshold — this acts as a noise filter to prevent the network from learning from price fluctuations around zero.
//+------------------------------------------------------------------+
//| Generating a label for a training example at bar index shift.    |
//| Returns 1 if the price is higher after InpMlpHorizon bars,       |
//| otherwise 0. Filters out noise using InpLabelMinPts.             |
