Pitfalls of Training in the Terminal
The cost of a run in the optimizer
. The network is retrained every InpRetrainBars bars, and each training session consists of InpMlpEpochs passes through the dataset. During optimization in the Strategy Tester, this is multiplied by the number of parameter combinations. If the run is slow, increase InpRetrainBars or decrease InpMlpEpochs or InpMlpLookback. For live trading, speed isn't important (one training session every few hundred bars), but for large-scale optimization, it is very important.
Determinism
. He initialization uses MathRand. Without controlling the seed, two runs on the same data may yield slightly different weights and different trades. MathSrand fixes the sequence of random numbers within a given run; to reproduce a test exactly, you can replace TimeCurrent() with a constant seed, while for a statistically robust assessment, you should run several sessions with different seeds and examine the variability rather than a single successful run.
Look-ahead bias
. This is a common mistake in indicators: the feature on a bar is calculated using future bars. In our Expert Advisor, features are taken strictly from closed bars (inference uses shift=1), while training labels look ahead only within historical data that is already available. At the live edge of the chart, future data does not exist and is not used. It is important to keep this distinction in mind whenever modifying features.
Class imbalance
. If the numbers of upward and downward movements for an instrument differ substantially during the training period, the network will be biased toward the more frequent class. The InpLabelMinPts noise filter partially addresses this by filtering out small movements; if there is a significant imbalance, you should add class weighting in Step.
Quick Backtest Check
After enabling the MLP gate, evaluate the results not only in terms of profit, but also drawdown behavior, the number of trades, the proportion of rejected candidates, and stability across different historical periods. In one of the tests, the system performs quite well — and the risk manager provides protection by closing problematic series of trades in time:
